<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rani Mangammal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1705</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rani Mangammal was queen regent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> kingdom from about 1689 to 1704, on behalf of her grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijaya-ranga-chokkanatha">Vijaya Ranga Chokkanatha</a>. She kept the kingdom intact through diplomacy with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and Travancore. She is remembered for building roads, rest houses, water tanks and choultries across the southern Tamil country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rani-mangammal.jpg" alt="Rani Mangammal" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suresh, Madurai · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tirumalai_Nayak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
